# Vendored game assemblies — never commit game code.
#
# ⚠️ NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is load-bearing rather than style. A
# directory-only pattern (`vendor/`) does NOT match a SYMLINK, so in a lane
# worktree — where these are symlinked back to the main checkout because a bare
# worktree cannot build without them — `git add -A` STAGES THE LINK, committing
# this machine's absolute path, home directory and username included. Measured
# 2026-08-22 in a throwaway repo, with a positive control proving the check could
# see staging at all: `vendor/` staged the link, `vendor` did not.
#
# The previous mitigation was "commit by explicit path", which is a discipline
# that has to hold on every commit in every concurrent lane. This makes git
# actually ignore the thing. Guarded by tools/gitignore-symlink-check.sh.
# (Same discovery path as the sister project, which hit it first and told us.)
vendor

# Decompiled reference output — never commit. No trailing slash: see vendor above.
decompiled
decompiled-firstpass

# Cloned third-party reference mods — not ours to commit. No trailing slash: see vendor.
references

# Local machine-specific build config
*.local.props
GamePath.props

# Build output
bin/
obj/
dist/

# Project-local NuGet cache (shared ~/.nuget has container-ownership issues).
# No trailing slash: see vendor — this one is 416M and is symlinked into every lane.
.packages

# Test artifacts
coverage.json
TestResults/

# Captured Player.log files — they carry public IPs, machine names and the
# Windows account name of whoever was testing. Redact into docs/notes/ instead;
# see stage2-run-2026-08-02.md for the shape.
logs/

# Playtest run logs (tools/playtest-m12b.sh)
.playtest/

# Python bytecode from tools/split (its modules import each other).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
